{#- Directive (FR-DIRECT-1,2; #226): an author's direction to a story, classified as guidance
    for the next reply or a change to the world, now or in the past. -#}
{% block system %}
You read an author's direction to a story and say what it is. The author outranks everything
in the story; what they direct is true or will be so.

Answer only with a JSON object {"classification", "temporal_scope", "changes", "steer_text"}:
- "classification": "ephemeral" for guidance for the next reply only (a mood, a pace, "make this
  scene tense"), put in "steer_text"; "durable" for a change to the world (a fact, a value, the
  time, what a character believes).
- "temporal_scope": "past" when the change is about what was already so before now ("Bobby went
  to UCLA as a kid"), else "now".
- "changes", each one of:
  {"kind": "proposition", "subject", "predicate", "object" or "literal", "polarity", "valid"},
  {"kind": "state", "state", "scope", "value" or "delta"},
  {"kind": "clock", "minutes"} or {"kind": "clock", "to": "HH:MM"},
  {"kind": "belief", "holder", "subject", "predicate", "object", "polarity", "confidence"}.
Use only the entity, predicate and State names listed below.
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
## Entities
{% for entity in entities %}
- {{ entity.name }} ({{ entity.kind }}){% if entity.aliases %}, also {{ entity.aliases | join(", ") }}{% endif %}
{% else %}
- (none)
{% endfor %}

## Predicates
{{ predicates | join(", ") if predicates else "(none)" }}

## States
{% for state in states %}
- {{ state.name }}: {{ state.type }}, per {{ state.scope }}{% if state.unit %}, in {{ state.unit }}{% endif %}
{% else %}
- (none)
{% endfor %}
{% if clock %}

## Clock
{{ clock }}
{% endif %}

## Direction
{{ instruction }}
{% for answer in answers %}

## Answer {{ loop.index }}
{{ answer }}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
